      "writtenOn": "2025-01-06T10:33:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As mentioned in [the other comment](https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/packages/modules/Virtualization/+/3399546/comment/0c30901e_5c443b11/), this is not enough to ensure safety.\n\nRust raw pointers can point to a place in memory where the data _used_ to be. That is, a `Guid` value existed there a few milliseconds ago, but it has since then been deallocated. The pointers to the old data will stick around and it is undefined behavior if such a pointer is dereferenced.\n\nBasically, since a pointer is just an integer, you cannot know if it is valid from looking at the pointer alone. The `non_null_and_aligned_const` function should probably be removed since it provides a false sense of security.",
